A||||8||ChadMan||Northstars and Nationals!
Z||000000||ChadMan||08-16-99||07:26 AM||||Good turnout at this year's Fiero Festival.  Lots of nice custom and stock Fieros, but what really impressed me were the four Northstar cars that showed up.  The coolest of these (IMHO) was Jonathan Watts' "Purple Rain".  It had 18" Boyd Coddington wheels, leather interior, giant fender flares, purple color-shifting paint, and of course the Northstar.  When he fired that bad boy up and gunned it, people's heads turned for about 300 feet in any direction!  Other Northstars: John Norman's "Obsession" with a new paint job, Chris Moore's fastback GT in navy blue, and a guy with a stock-looking Formula that looked like a work in progress, but probably runs 13-sec quarters.<p>There was also El Fiero with the longitudinally-mounted 305 TPI V8 (see post in Tech section).<p>Oh yeah, and I won a second-place trophy with my 88 Coupe, though I must say it's not a highly-contested class.<p>Hope to see all of you at Louisville, KY next year!
Z||000001||BluByYou||08-16-99||01:04 PM||||Chadman - How did you like Chris Moore's Northstar?  He's a buddy of mine.  Between him and his brother, they have 6 Fieros.  Chris alone has two '88 GT's, a mint '87 GT, the Northstar and a Formula!  He spent a lot of time and money on his Northstar, though - from the ground up.  It's really a looker AND screamer!  I enjoy hangin' with him - can ya imagine that?<br>  <IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15>
Z||000002||Eric||08-16-99||08:24 PM||||When did you guys see all these cars.  I went there on Friday afternoon and Saturday at about 3:00PM, there was nothing but a few (30-40) cars.  It only took me about 20 minutes to see every car in the lot and talk with some of the owners.  Did I show up at the wrong time?  I didn't have a car to show on account of my rebuild project, so I didn't bother to figure out when the "best" times to come were.  I hope to have a nice modified 88GT to bring next year.  I'm glad to hear the show won't be too far away.
Z||000003||biggdaddy||08-16-99||11:28 PM||||Does anyone know if and when pics from this show will get online?  I`m kinda far away (Montreal) but would like to see all these cool cars.
Z||000004||spike||08-17-99||07:33 AM||||I am also from Montreal. Are there any Fiero events close to home. Does anyone know if a Montreal Fiero Club exist. It would be a blast if all us "Montrealers" can take a cruise next summer to participate in some of the many events held in the States. As far as I know there is nothing much here going on. Maybe next summer when I get my Fiero I will start a Montreal Fiero Club. I wonder how many people in Montreal how Fieros.
Z||000005||ChadMan||08-17-99||07:41 AM||||Chris is a cool guy.  I met him at the 1996 Festival in Indy (my first) and he had some good helpful advice on how to fix my then-sputtering 88 Coupe.  His Northstar is kick-ass - the color is beautiful.  I didn't get to talk with him much at the show b/c I was working with COFE, our local chapter.<p>People started bringing out cars at 9 am and judging wrapped up at 2, so Eric, you probably missed the best cars.  The weather was nasty!  Well, there's always Louisville in 2000.<p>Photos from the show should be up on the Central Ohio Fiero Enthusiasts site sometime within the next couple of weeks.  The URL is www.ohiofiero.com.  (I don't know how to make it a link - sorry)
Z||000006||RossT||08-18-99||12:58 AM||||I would also like to put my 2 cents in about Chris.  About six months ago, when I first started looking for a fiero, I had contacted <br>Chris, cause he had a car for sale.  While he had already sold the car, he spent about and hour on the phone with me, a complete stranger, talking about fiero's.  Chris was the first real fiero person that I had ever talked to.  (he gave me the "fiero<br>bug")  Thanks Chris.<p>Ross
